Package: vaevictis-hardening
Version: 1.3.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: linuxtuts-website <292920559+linuxtuts-website@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: systemd
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://vaevictisos.org
Description: VaeVictis 1.3 settings for SSH, the firewall, the kernel and Firefox
 For systems installed from VaeVictis OS 1.1 or 1.2: puts the settings of 1.3
 in place of the files those images installed, only where a file is exactly
 what VaeVictis shipped (a file changed locally is left alone, with a message):
 .
  - SSH (switched off by default): ed25519 keys only, no sftp, post-quantum
    key exchange first. Not applied while any authorized key is not ed25519
    (or while certificates or an AuthorizedKeysCommand are used), so nobody
    is locked out: the message says what to do.
  - firewall: the SSH port open only while SSH runs, at most 4 new SSH
    connections a minute from one address, impossible TCP flag combinations
    dropped.
  - kernel: the strict reverse-path filter on the VPN tunnel and the virtual
    networks (NetworkManager keeps the connection to the internet loose).
  - Firefox ESR: system policies (no telemetry, no studies, strict tracking
    protection, no sponsored content), only if there are none yet.
 .
 What is not installed (an SSH server, nftables, Firefox) is skipped, never
 installed. The replaced files are kept in /var/lib/vaevictis-hardening/backup.
 Removing this package does not restore them.
 .
 A Debian-based hobby project: its own tools are written with AI assistants
 and not independently audited. Provided as is, without warranty (GPL-3.0).
 Part of VaeVictis OS.
